    "Badger ultrasonic flow meter BACnet"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Ultrasonic flow and BTU meter (BACnet MS/TP)",
  "applies_to": "Badger Meter Dynasonics TFX-5000 clamp-on ultrasonic flow meters and TFX-5000 energy (BTU) meters, using the built-in RS-485 port in BACnet MS/TP mode.",
  "summary": "The TFX-5000's RS-485 port can run Modbus RTU or BACnet MS/TP. In BACnet MS/TP mode it serves flow rate, velocity and totalizer Analog Values in home-screen, US and metric units, 64-bit Large Analog Value copies of each total, Multi-state Values that report the selected units, three writable cutoff settings, and four Binary Output actions (reset totals, unlatch alarms, clear alarm history, reboot). Energy meters add energy rate, two temperatures, delta T and energy totals. This list is the energy-meter table; flow-only meters have the same objects minus the energy and temperature ones.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "02.02.536 (PICS)",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Flow-only meters lack AV 604-607, AV 802, AV 1002, the energy totals and counters (AV 2308-2315, 2408-2415, 2508-2515 and their LAV copies) and MV 3006, 3008, 3009.",
    "Totals come as 32-bit AVs plus 64-bit LAV copies (LAV 2600-2811); use the LAV if the BMS supports it, since large totals lose resolution in 32 bits.",
    "Values marked 'home-screen units' follow the units chosen for the meter display; MV 3000-3009 report which units are selected.",
    "Several overflow counters share the name 'Totalizer Overflow Counter (...)'; the instance tells them apart.",
    "The manual lists failure, check-function and warning codes, but the object list has no alarm or error-code object.",
    "Source is user manual TTM-UM-03074-EN-07 (January 2026)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "TFX-5000 Meter BACnet MS/TP Protocol User Manual",
    "doc_number": "TTM-UM-03074-EN-07",
    "revision_date": "2026-01",
    "url": "https://badgermeter.widen.net/content/8nc9jpqgfl/original?download=false&x.app=api"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Select BACnet MS/TP in the meter's communication menu, set the MAC address and BACnet ID, and match baud, parity and stop bits. Read flow rate and totals (and energy rate, temperatures and energy totals on BTU meters). Use the 64-bit LAV totals where possible. Writes (cutoffs and the BO actions) need the Access setting at read/write.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 600",
        "name": "Flow Rate on Screen",
        "why": "Flow rate, home-screen units"
      },
      {
        "ref": "LAV 2600",
        "name": "Net Flow Totalizer",
        "why": "Net volume total, 64-bit"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 604",
        "name": "Energy/BTU Rate",
        "why": "Energy rate (BTU meters)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 605",
        "name": "Temperature #1",
        "why": "Temperature 1 (BTU meters)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 606",
        "name": "Temperature #2",
        "why": "Temperature 2 (BTU meters)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "LAV 2608",
        "name": "Energy/BTU Net Total",
        "why": "Net energy total, 64-bit (BTU meters)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 5500",
        "name": "Signal Strength",
        "why": "Ultrasonic signal strength"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Main Menu > System Setup > Communication: select BACnet MS/TP, set the MAC address (1-254) and BACnet ID (0-4194303).",
      "Baud rate, parity, stop bits and max MAC address must match the network.",
      "A built-in terminating resistor can be switched on in the communication settings for the last device on the trunk.",
      "The Access setting chooses read-only or read/write for the network; writes fail when it is read-only.",
      "Up to 126 transmitters on one RS-485 trunk of up to 4000 ft; the port detects swapped A/B wires."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Flow and total values are in the home-screen units unless you use the fixed-unit objects (gal/min, l/min, gal, liters, kBTU, kWh).",
      "Reset Totalizers clears every flow total in the meter.",
      "Flow-only meters do not have the energy and temperature objects.",
      "When a USB programming cable is connected, the RS-485 port is disabled."
    ]
  },
